FIX: MySQL Not Starting in XAMPP

This guide helps you reinitialize your MySQL data folder and restore your databases.

PART 1: BACKUP

1. Stop MySQL from XAMPP:
   - Open XAMPP Control Panel
   - Click "Stop" on MySQL

2. Backup Current Data:
   - Go to: C:\\xampp\\mysql\\
   - Copy the "data" folder and save it somewhere safe as "data-backup"

PART 2: REINITIALIZE MYSQL

1. Delete the current "data" folder from: C:\\xampp\\mysql\\

2. Copy default data:
   - Go to: C:\\xampp\\mysql\\backup
   - Copy all contents, paste into: C:\\xampp\\mysql\\
   - Rename it as "data"

3. Start MySQL:
   - Open XAMPP as Administrator
   - Click "Start" on MySQL

PART 3: RESTORE OLD DATABASES

1. From your "data-backup", copy only your project folders (e.g., gym_system, student_mgmt)
   - DO NOT copy mysql/, phpmyadmin/, performance_schema/, information_schema/

2. Paste copied folders into: C:\\xampp\\mysql\\data

3. (If using InnoDB):
   - Copy ibdata1 file from data-backup to the new data folder

4. Set folder permissions:
   - Right-click on data folder > Properties > Security > Grant Full Control

PART 4: FINAL CHECK

1. Restart MySQL in XAMPP
2. Go to http://localhost/phpmyadmin
3. Check if your databases are visible and working

TROUBLESHOOTING:

- MySQL not starting: Check mysql_error.log in C:\\xampp\\mysql\\data
- Unknown table engine 'InnoDB': ibdata1 is missing or corrupted
- Tables not found: Missing .frm or .ibd files
- Can't open tables: Incomplete InnoDB backup

SUMMARY:

1. Backup your MySQL data folder
2. Replace with clean data folder from backup/
3. Start MySQL cleanly
4. Restore only project database folders
5. Restart MySQL and check in phpMyAdmin
"""
